//! The `rule-overlap` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property specifies
//! which rule is painted on top when column rules and row rules intersect.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - column-over-row: Specifies that column rules are painted over row rules.
//! - row-over-column: Specifies that row rules are painted over column rules. This is the default
//! value.
//!
//! Grammar: row-over-column | column-over-row
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-gaps-1/#propdef-rule-overlap
